# The rules of lab/profile/fold.php: which step of a request a frame of a profile belongs to. A sample takes the step of its LEAF
# (innermost) frame, and only that one: a leaf no `step` rule names is "unclassified", whatever its callers are. So every PHP function
# that can be the innermost frame of a sample needs a rule here, and a renamed or new function shows up as unclassified.
#
#   step  <frame> <step>            a frame is its name in the collapsed stacks; a trailing * makes it a prefix
#   route <frame> <endpoint name>   the endpoint a sample belongs to: the route function found on its stack (any depth); a sample with
#                                   none is "shared" (reading, parsing, writing, the loop: work done before the route is known)
#
# Steps: S1 accept and close connections, S2 read and parse the request, S3 route, S4 verify the JWT, S5 validate the input, S6 query
# SQLite, S7 build the JSON, S8 write the response, S9 durability, loop = the event loop's own code.
#
# What a frame holds, and why (Excimer takes a sample at the next VM interrupt check, and an internal function is never a frame of its
# own: its time is the calling PHP function's, and the time spent in libevent between two callbacks lands on the next callback's frame;
# lab/README.md has the calibration that shows it):
#
# - DiyServer::onReadable and ::onWritable hold almost no PHP of their own: their own samples are libevent's dispatch and epoll_wait's
#   kernel time (the loop), and DiyServer::settle adds and removes events (libevent calls): loop.
# - DiyServer::onAccept holds stream_socket_accept and the setup of the new socket: S1, like DiyConnection::close (fclose).
# - Group commit (APP_GROUP_COMMIT=1): DiyServer::turn, ::flush and the grouped callbacks are the loop's own code (the flush calls the
#   commit and answers the connections: what is in them is the other frames'); DiyConnection::takePending and ::resume are glue: loop.
#   app_group_commit is the one frame with S9 work: BEGIN IMMEDIATE, the savepoints and COMMIT run in its own PDOStatement::execute calls
#   (the write's statement runs in post_insert or like_insert: S6, as without the switch). A write's closure is the app's glue: S3.
# - DiyConnection::onReadable holds fread (the kernel's receive path is in the syscall): S2, like parse and parseHead. parse also
#   holds the concatenation of the response head and body, which is S8 work, too small to split without a function of its own.
# - DiyConnection::advance and ::onWritable hold fwrite (the kernel's send path): S8. DiyConnection::respond is the concatenation that
#   used to be inside parse (the response head and body): S2, so a profile before and after the split reads the same.
# - S9 has no frame without group commit: SQLite commits inside PDOStatement::execute (autocommit), so a write's commit and its WAL
#   checkpoint are in the write query function, S6. The row stays in the table, at 0, to say so; with group commit it is app_group_commit.
# - route_health runs its query inline (no query function of its own), so its own samples are S6.
# - app_count only counts the request for the telemetry (off in a profile) and hands the response back: it is the router's glue, S3.
# - DiyProfile::write is the profiler's own flush (stop, merge, rewrite the file), run by a timer on the loop between two requests.
#   It is not a step of a request: it goes to the event loop, with the timer's closure and the small calls of a connection that the
#   loop makes (the questions `settle` asks). It was 0.03 % of the samples in the baseline. A closure of another file is not named:
#   a closure of the app would be unclassified, which is what a new piece of code should be.

step DiyServer::run loop
step DiyServer::onReadable loop
step DiyServer::onWritable loop
step DiyServer::settle loop
step DiyServer::turn loop
step DiyServer::flush loop
step DiyServer::onReadableGrouped loop
step DiyServer::onWritableGrouped loop
step DiyServer::settleGrouped loop
step DiyConnection::takePending loop
step DiyConnection::resume loop
step DiyConnection::wantsRead loop
step DiyConnection::wantsWrite loop
step DiyConnection::pendingBytes loop
step DiyProfile::start loop
step DiyProfile::write loop
step DiyProfile::merge loop
step {closure:/lab/servers/diy-profile.php* loop
step DiyServer::onAccept S1
step DiyConnection::close S1
step DiyConnection::__construct S1
step DiyPeer::__construct S1
step DiyConnection::onReadable S2
step DiyConnection::parse S2
step DiyConnection::parseHead S2
step DiyConnection::respond S2
step DiyConnection::reject S2
step handler_handle S3
step app_count S3
step route_post_get S3
step route_post_create S3
step route_like S3
step post_create S3
step like_create S3
step {closure:/lab/app/app.php* S3
step app_group_commit S9
step route_feed S3
step route_health S6
step jwt_verify S4
step jwt_base64url_decode S4
step id_validate S5
step body_validate S5
step feed_query S6
step post_query S6
step post_insert S6
step post_exists S6
step like_insert S6
step feed_json S7
step post_json S7
step like_json S7
step health_json S7
step health_degraded_json S7
step response_json S8
step response_error S8
step DiyConnection::advance S8
step DiyConnection::onWritable S8

route route_health GET /health
route route_feed GET /feed
route route_post_get GET /posts/:id
route route_post_create POST /posts
route route_like POST /posts/:id/like
route post_create POST /posts
route like_create POST /posts/:id/like
